Clippy is clean. Let's do a final full run of both new acceptance suites plus the required `tests-green-crates` package set, to confirm nothing regressed elsewhere.
Everything is green. Summary of the remediation:

**F1 (unverified new tests)** — Ran `cargo test --workspace` against the base state and found the actual failure hidden inside the failed `tests-workspace-advisory` run: `shared_scope_without_a_declared_dependency_still_serializes` (one of the new PRD-38 tests) panicked with a git "Author identity unknown" error. It's the only test in the new suite that drives real review + real git integration commits without persisting a local git identity — every other test in the file either disables review or goes through a fake `CommandRunner`. Fixed by adding `git config user.email`/`user.name` to that test's fixture repo (matching the codebase's existing convention in `worktree.rs`/`resume.rs`/`run.rs`), so it no longer depends on ambient global git config. Reproduced the original failure and the fix by running with `GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=/dev/null GIT_CONFIG_SYSTEM=/dev/null` (simulating the rootless Docker container) — confirmed all 13 daemon tests and all 4 MCP tests now pass hermetically. (The other 3 failures in that run — two `run::tests::*` and `autonomous_delivery.rs`'s `shared_scope_wave_completes_end_to_end_through_drive_alone` — are pre-existing, unrelated to this diff, and out of scope for this remediation.)

**F2 (scope violation)** — Relocated everything that lived outside `crates/`:
- `tests/fixtures/{repo-rust-cli,repo-node-service}/` → `crates/familiar-ai-daemon/tests/fixtures/` (single checked-in copy; the MCP suite now points its `copy_fixture_repository` at `../familiar-ai-daemon/tests/fixtures` instead of duplicating content)
- `docs/acceptance/PRD-038-multi-repo-have-at-it.md` → `crates/familiar-ai-daemon/tests/acceptance/PRD-038-multi-repo-have-at-it.md`, with its fixture-location prose updated

Verified: `git diff --name-status` shows every changed path now resolves under `crates/`; `cargo build --workspace` shows no workspace-membership warnings from the nested fixture `Cargo.toml`; `cargo fmt --all -- --check` and `cargo clippy -p familiar-ai-daemon -p familiar-ai-mcp --all-targets -- -D warnings` are both clean.

No commits were made — the working tree is left with these unstaged changes for review.
